## Data Flow — BigQuery → S3 → Redshift

```
BigQuery (google-cloud-bigquery client)
        │
        │  1. SELECT * from `project.dataset.table`
        │     using bigquery_connector.build_query()
        │
        ↓
  Pandas / PyArrow DataFrame in Python memory
        │
        │  2. Serialize to chosen format:
        │     Parquet → fastparquet / pyarrow
        │     JSON    → df.to_json()
        │     ORC     → pyarrow ORC writer
        │     Iceberg → pyiceberg (S3-only route only)
        │
        ↓
  bytes in memory (io.BytesIO buffer)
        │
        │  3. boto3 s3_client.put_object()
        │
        ↓
  s3://bucket/prefix/dataset/table_timestamp.parquet
        │
        │  4. (S3 → Redshift route only)
        │     Redshift Data API COPY command
        │     via bigquery_migration.load_to_redshift()
        │
        ↓
  Redshift table (rs_schema.rs_table)
```

**Key differences vs Snowflake route:**
- BQ uses `FORMAT AS PARQUET/JSON/ORC` — no `FORMAT AS ICEBERG` in Redshift COPY
- BQ uses Redshift Data API (async) with idempotency tokens — resumable by design
- Iceberg format is only available on the BQ → S3 only route (not BQ → Redshift)

